  "answer_text": "Currently, Telangana has the following number of MLA and MP seats:\n\n### **Current Seat Counts**\n* **MLA (Member of Legislative Assembly) Seats:** **119**\n* **MP (Member of Parliament) Seats:** **24** total\n  * **Lok Sabha (Lower House):** 17 seats\n  * **Rajya Sabha (Upper House):** 7 seats\n* **MLC (Member of Legislative Council) Seats:** **40** (Telangana has a bicameral legislature)\n\n---\n\n### **Proposed Future Changes (Delimitation Bill, 2026)**\nWith the introduction of the *Delimitation Bill, 2026* by the Indian government, Telangana is projected to see a significant expansion in its political boundaries for future elections (expected to take effect starting with the 2029 general elections):\n\n* **Proposed MLA Seats:** Expected to increase from 119 to **179** (an increase of 60 seats).\n* **Proposed Lok Sabha MP Seats:** Expected to increase from 17 to **26** (an increase of 9 seats).",
